From 91965661b8347e2f64080a5f3d33caff8e072eac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Moskowski <me@corpix.ru>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 05:05:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] support AmneziaWG 3 device settings

Adds HeaderProtectionKey, ContentPaddingAddition, RekeyAfterTime,
RekeyTimeout, RejectAfterTime, KeepaliveTimeout, MaxHandshakeAttempts,
RandomTrailers and DisableCookies to the config file, the set arguments,
show, showconf and the cross-platform uapi protocol.

The six timing settings and ContentPaddingAddition are u16 ranges,
spelled "N" or "lo-hi" like H1-H4 and PersistentKeepalive, parsed by a
shared parse_u16_range and printed by u16_range_spec.
HeaderProtectionKey follows PrivateKey: base64 in a config file, a file
path on the command line, and masked in show output.

H1-H4 are now validated when the config is parsed rather than at the
netlink boundary, so a reversed range is reported as a configuration
error with the rest of the input checks. The boundary check stays as a
guard and now sets errno, since perror was reporting "Success".

The fork does not document the AmneziaWG settings in the man pages or
shell completions, so these are not added there either.
